<title>UK: NTT sets $500 million five-year bond.</title>
<headline>NTT sets $500 million five-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced</p>
<p>by joint lead managers Goldman Sachs and SBC Warburg.</p>
<p> BORROWER   NIPPON TELEGRAPH AND TELEPHONE CORP</p>
<p> AMT    $500 MLN	COUPON     **	  MATURITY    16.MAY.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  **	  PAY DATE    16.MAY.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.875     REOFFER    **	  SPREAD	+9 BP</p>
<p> NOTES   ** TO BE PRICED</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LONDON    PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK/JP</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  JAPAN     TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.25	SELL CONC  1.65	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 2002 U.S. TREASURY NOTE</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
